    <DataNode elementId="RX" textLabel="RX" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="C01322" dataSource="KEGG Compound" />
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="1660" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco">RX stands for endogenous or xenobiotic, often toxic, electrophilic chemical compounds that enter a living organism and can be degraded by glutathione &lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-transferase enzymes. R may be an aliphatic, aromatic or heterocyclic group, while X may be a sulfate, nitrile or halide group.</Comment>
