      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco">|FRAME: RX| stands for endogenous or xenobiotic, often toxic, electrophilic chemical compounds that enter a living organism and can be degraded by glutathione &lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;-transferase enzymes. R may be an aliphatic, aromatic or heterocyclic group, while X may be a sulfate, nitrile or halide group. The |FRAME: HX| compound describes the sulfate, nitrile or halide group after removal of the R group.</Comment>
